      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "← every box carries one of these: LIVE = running on devnet now · BUILT · gated = deployed, waiting on an external key · IN PROGRESS = being written today · PLANNED · RETIRED / DROPPED (removed 21 Sep) · ROADMAP (after the hackathon) · CORE = the mechanism itself",
      "originalText": "← every box carries one of these: LIVE = running on devnet now · BUILT · gated = deployed, waiting on an external key · IN PROGRESS = being written today · PLANNED · RETIRED / DROPPED (removed 21 Sep) · ROADMAP (after the hackathon) · CORE = the mechanism itself",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "t.what",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 132,
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 195,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1f2937",
      "backgroundColor": "#f3f4f6",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "g.t.what"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": null,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "seed": 315360601,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1407480935,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "t.what.t"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "t.what.t",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 28,
      "y": 140,
      "width": 999,
      "height": 179,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1f2937",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "g.t.what"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 572073246,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 55440893,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "WHAT THIS PRODUCT DOES — in plain words\nSome people hold tokenized stocks (a Solana token that tracks a real share, e.g. TSLAx tracks Tesla). Some people hold USDC.\nTHE WINDOW lets the stock holders BORROW USDC overnight against their stock, and the USDC holders LEND it — at ONE interest\nrate per round, found by an auction. That rate is published every round as xONIA (\"xStocks Overnight Index Average\"): the\nfirst on-chain benchmark borrow rate for tokenized equities, like SOFR or SONIA are for dollars and pounds.\nThe twist: how much anyone lends, borrows or pledges is NEVER visible on chain. Amounts travel as encrypted numbers, the chain\nadds them up while still encrypted, and an administrator who CAN decrypt the totals must PROVE every total it publishes.\nThe loan is safe because the borrower proves — without showing the numbers — that the stock pledged is worth at least 150 %\nof the loan at the current price from a public price feed (Pyth). No fresh price → no loan can start and no loan can be seized.\nWhat is public: who took part, at which rate, the round's totals, the rate, the price. What is private: every individual amount.\nOn devnet the stocks are mock twins, the administrator is one disclosed key, and the auction depth comes from labelled bots.",
      "originalText": "WHAT THIS PRODUCT DOES — in plain words\nSome people hold tokenized stocks (a Solana token that tracks a real share, e.g. TSLAx tracks Tesla). Some people hold USDC.\nTHE WINDOW lets the stock holders BORROW USDC overnight against their stock, and the USDC holders LEND it — at ONE interest\nrate per round, found by an auction. That rate is published every round as xONIA (\"xStocks Overnight Index Average\"): the\nfirst on-chain benchmark borrow rate for tokenized equities, like SOFR or SONIA are for dollars and pounds.\nThe twist: how much anyone lends, borrows or pledges is NEVER visible on chain. Amounts travel as encrypted numbers, the chain\nadds them up while still encrypted, and an administrator who CAN decrypt the totals must PROVE every total it publishes.\nThe loan is safe because the borrower proves — without showing the numbers — that the stock pledged is worth at least 150 %\nof the loan at the current price from a public price feed (Pyth). No fresh price → no loan can start and no loan can be seized.\nWhat is public: who took part, at which rate, the round's totals, the rate, the price. What is private: every individual amount.\nOn devnet the stocks are mock twins, the administrator is one disclosed key, and the auction depth comes from labelled bots.",
