    {
      "id": "rm.amend.t",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3088,
      "y": 5232,
      "width": 492,
      "height": 228,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1f2937",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "g.rm.amend"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 456658402,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1585570134,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "WHAT CHANGED WHILE BUILDING — the\n  amendments (SPEC_AMENDMENTS.md)\nThe print is batched into begin / attest / finalize because\nproofs must fit in transactions (A1). One account per bid (A2).\nUnits fixed to milli-shares, cents and a milli-factor (A3).\nWrapping needs no proof (A4); a deposit is checked by looking\nat the transfer beside it (A5). Full fills reuse the bid's\nciphertext (A6). The split factor is read from the token (A7).\nA newer proof library was required after a transcript change\n(A10). The price moved from a keyed web API to Pyth's on-chain\naccount (A11), then gained an on-chain \"quote too old\" rule\n(A13), then a schedule of several collaterals (A14), then a\nlisting that reads Pyth's account directly (A15). Program size\nis budgeted because rent is paid forever (A12).",
      "originalText": "WHAT CHANGED WHILE BUILDING — the\n  amendments (SPEC_AMENDMENTS.md)\nThe print is batched into begin / attest / finalize because\nproofs must fit in transactions (A1). One account per bid (A2).\nUnits fixed to milli-shares, cents and a milli-factor (A3).\nWrapping needs no proof (A4); a deposit is checked by looking\nat the transfer beside it (A5). Full fills reuse the bid's\nciphertext (A6). The split factor is read from the token (A7).\nA newer proof library was required after a transcript change\n(A10). The price moved from a keyed web API to Pyth's on-chain\naccount (A11), then gained an on-chain \"quote too old\" rule\n(A13), then a schedule of several collaterals (A14), then a\nlisting that reads Pyth's account directly (A15). Program size\nis budgeted because rent is paid forever (A12).",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "rm.amend",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
